Renter's Handbook
TLC Inspection
Before the TLC Inspection, Check:
that all required TLC stickers are present and in good condition;
the exterior lights;
seat belts;
tire condition;
the suspension and braking system;
the condition and operation of the WAV ramp and other
equipment used to transport wheelchair passengers;
the backup alarm. If the vehicle has a separate alarm switch, make
sure the alarm is on before the inspection.
 WAV RAMP
 REVERSE
 ALARM ON
The vehicle must be fully prepared for the TLC inspection, with
no faults that could affect safety or the inspection result.
